From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: Start the next job from the interrupt thread

The decoder idled from a job's interrupt until the mem2mem worker woke
to start the next. The interrupt is threaded and can sleep: run the
next job there. On an RK3528 decoding HEVC at 3840x2160 the worker took
40 to 60 us of the 8.6 ms frame.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
index 534346a..f773208 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec.c
@@ -1689,8 +1689,12 @@ static irqreturn_t rkvdec_irq_handler(int irq, void *priv)
 	struct rkvdec_dev *rkvdec = priv;
 	struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx = v4l2_m2m_get_curr_priv(rkvdec->m2m_dev);
 	const struct rkvdec_variant *variant = rkvdec->variant;
+	irqreturn_t ret;
 
-	return variant->ops->irq_handler(ctx);
+	ret = variant->ops->irq_handler(ctx);
+	/* The decoder idles until the next job: start it here, not from a worker */
+	v4l2_m2m_run_next(rkvdec->m2m_dev);
+	return ret;
 }
 
